      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "US equities lost $3 trillion in one session as AI and chip stocks sold off after the midterms.\n\nThe Nasdaq 100 fell 6.3% and the S&P 500 dropped 4.3%. $NVDA slid 9.0%, $MSFT 3.5%, and $GOOGL 2.3%. Data center stocks fell further: $IREN 16.0%, $NBIS 15.1%, and $CIFR 14.6%.\n\nThe plunge ended a post-midterm rally, the strongest in 44 years. Crypto followed, with $BTC down 6.4% and $ETH down 7.9% at their lows.\n\nWith Democrats controlling Congress, markets are weighing tougher AI regulation. Rep. Yassamin Ansari proposed pausing advanced AI and banning superintelligence. Senator Sanders called for a national data center moratorium, and Wall Street is pricing in a major slowdown in AI infrastructure growth.\n\nMoonDust Chronicles",
