      "text": "US equities lost $3 trillion in a single session as a sell-off in AI and chip stocks sent markets tumbling after the midterms.\n\nThe Nasdaq 100 fell 6.3%, while the S&P 500 dropped 4.3%. Nvidia slid 9.0%; Microsoft lost 3.5%, and Alphabet 2.3%. Data center stocks were hit even harder: IREN fell 16.0%, NBIS 15.1%, and CIFR 14.6%.\n\nThe post-midterm rally, the strongest in 44 years, quickly faded. Bitcoin touched a low of -6.4%, while Ethereum reached -7.9%.\n\nBehind the reversal is a growing fear of tougher AI regulation. With Democrats now controlling Congress, Rep. Yassamin Ansari has proposed an immediate pause on advanced AI and a ban on superintelligence. Senator Sanders is also pushing for a national data center moratorium, and Wall Street is pricing in a significant slowdown in AI infrastructure spending.\n\nCrupto Meny\n\n#USMarkets #AIStocks #ChipStocks #Bitcoin #Ethereum",
